<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Boer War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1899">1899</a>–<a href="/years/1902">1902</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> War was fought from 1899 to 1902 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> and the two Boer republics, the South African Republic and the Orange Free State. After early setbacks, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> deployed large forces, used scorched-earth tactics and interned civilians in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camps</a>. Accounts of the British Empire present it as a costly victory that exposed military weaknesses and drew international criticism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-boer-war.jpg" alt="Second Boer War" width="320" height="332" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The British Army and The Illustrated London News · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Second_Boer_War_Collage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
